--- a/guild-idler-status.md
+++ b/guild-idler-status.md
@@ -22695,3 +22695,24 @@ Dev Update | Patch 0287
 **Hero name pool expansion.** Every one of the 13 classes in `hero-classes.json` had exactly 5 names -- confirmed directly from the data, and the reported Sir Corwin/Dame Orla collisions are exactly what a 5-name pool produces once a guild recruits more than a couple of heroes of the same class. Added 5 new, class-appropriate names to every class's own pool (5 -> 10 each: e.g. knight gains Sir Aldric/Dame Isolde/Sir Rowan/Dame Elowen/Sir Gavric; dwarf gains Borin/Freya Ironbrow/Dagna/Torvik/Old Hilde; full list in the diff), checked for no duplicate within any one class's own array before writing. Existing hero names on any current save are untouched -- this only widens the pool new recruits and rerolls draw from.
 
 **Verified:** `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx vite build --config vite.web.config.ts` both pass clean against a fresh clone with this patch applied. No `SAVE_VERSION` bump needed -- no `GameState`/`Hero` shape changed; `rerollName` only ever writes a string already valid at hero creation into the same `hero.name` field. Worth a real playtest: send a fresh guild's starter hero on their first quest a few times (seed-dependent, so confirm across a couple of saves) to see it never fail, and try Reroll Name a few times on a hero to confirm it never silently repeats the same name back-to-back.
+
+
+### "Try this next" quest-card shimmer: tutorial quest, then the first burst quest after it (patch 0288)
+
+```discord-update
+Dev Update | Patch 0288
+- Added: the first quest now glows with the same gold shimmer border a nav tab gets when it has something new -- impossible to miss as the thing to do first
+- Added: once that first quest is done, the shimmer moves to the first quick "burst" quest that turns up, nudging a new player toward trying one next
+```
+
+**Direct request**, building on patch 0287's starter-experience pass: reuse the existing "new item on a tab" gold shimmer (`.nav-tab-unread` in app.css, the rotating conic-gradient ring already used when a nav tab has an unread banner notification) as a card-level highlight instead -- first on the scripted tutorial quest itself, then, once that's done, on the first burst-mode quest offer to turn up, as a "try this next" nudge.
+
+**Reused the exact shimmer, not a lookalike.** `.nav-tab-unread::after`'s conic-gradient ring already exists purely as CSS (the registered `--nav-tab-shimmer-angle` custom property plus the `nav-tab-shimmer-rotate` keyframe), driven by `isNavTabUnread` (attention.ts) for the nav bar. Added a sibling rule, `.raid-card.quest-card-spotlight::after`, sharing the same custom property and keyframe (so the rotation and gradient stops are byte-identical, not a second shimmer that could subtly drift out of sync) -- only the ring's own thickness and `border-radius` differ, sized for a full quest card (`border-radius: inherit` picks up `.card`'s own `var(--radius)` automatically) instead of a small square tab button.
+
+**Tutorial quest.** `QuestRow` (QuestPanel.tsx, the shared card component for a hero's own Quests & Contracts list) now adds `quest-card-spotlight` whenever `offer.id === TUTORIAL_QUEST_ID`. No new state needed -- `tutorialQuestOffer` is a single hardcoded offer only ever placed once, directly into the starter hero's own board (SaveManager.createInitialState), and it disappears the moment it's sent -- so the shimmer just derives straight off the offer id and clears itself for free.
+
+**The second quest -- first burst offer after completion.** This one does need new state, since "has the tutorial quest already been completed" doesn't derive from anything else in GameState. New `GameState.pendingBurstQuestSpotlight: boolean` (SAVE_VERSION 54 -> 55, migration 54 added -- defaults `false` for every existing save; see the field's own comment in types.ts for why a save already well past the tutorial quest has nothing left to retroactively arm this from). Set `true` the instant the tutorial quest resolves (`QuestManager.resolve`, right where `isTutorialQuest` is already known), cleared back to `false` the instant a hero is actually sent on any burst-mode offer (`QuestManager.start`) -- the hint's done its job once the player's tried a burst quest at all, not only if it happened to be the exact offer instance that was shimmering. While the flag is armed, `QuestRow` adds the shimmer to *every* burst-mode offer currently on the board, not one pinned instance -- a board refresh can swap out any given offer before a player notices it, so this targets the whole burst *category* until acted on, the same "highlight the whole tab, not one specific notification" shape `.nav-tab-unread` itself already uses.
+
+**New shared `QuestManager.isBurstOffer(offer)` helper**, needed to identify "is this a burst-mode offer" from the UI side for the spotlight check above. Found (and fixed) that this exact same determination -- `cfg.burstMaxDuration !== undefined && offer.duration <= cfg.burstMaxDuration` -- already existed as two *independent* inline copies inside `resolve()` (the daily-first-burst-bonus check, and the Grimsby-cooldown `isBurstQuest` check, the latter's own comment explicitly noting it was "computed independently here" from the former). Pulled all three into one helper rather than writing a third copy; `resolve()`'s two prior inline checks now call it too, with no behavior change -- confirmed identical by construction (byte-identical condition, just centralized).
+
+**Verified:** `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx vite build --config vite.web.config.ts` both pass clean against a fresh clone with this patch applied. `SAVE_VERSION` bumped 54 -> 55 for the new `pendingBurstQuestSpotlight` field -- migration 54 added, defaulting existing saves to `false` (a save already past the tutorial quest has nothing to arm this from anyway, per the field's own comment). Worth a real playtest: on a brand-new guild, confirm the tutorial quest card shimmers before it's sent, then confirm the shimmer picks up on the next burst-mode offer to appear (may take a board refresh or two, burst rolls at 45% on Easy) and clears the instant that offer -- or any other burst offer -- is actually sent.
